  "id": "COMPOUND:23719 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Tumidulin appears to have a complex relationship with DNA polymerase iota, as it is indirectly linked through multiple targets. The evidence suggests that Tumidulin acts as a target for CD276 antigen, which in turn targets Agosterol C2, and Agosterol C2 further targets DNA polymerase iota. This chain of interactions implies a potential pathway where Tumidulin influences DNA polymerase iota via CD276 and Agosterol C2. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with some variation in the strength of the connections. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Tumidulin modulates the activity of DNA polymerase iota through a series of molecular targets, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
